## Model change

- Chunk 4 (commit 420eb438): `savings_est = pixels * 1.0 / max(d, 1.0)`
- Chunk 5 (this commit):     `savings_est = pixels * 0.78 / sqrt(max(d, 1.0))`

## Geomean refit (20-cell sweep — patches_savings_calibrate_2026-05-17.tsv)

Distribution of empirical `actual_savings * sqrt(max(d,1.0)) / pixels`:
  min    = 0.265 (codec_wiki d=4.0)
  p25    = 0.544
  median = 0.676
  mean   = 0.901
  p75    = 1.339
  max    = 1.792 (windows95 d=4.0)
  geomean = 0.782 → rounded to C = 0.78

R² of constant predictor vs measured per-image variance:
  Old model (C=1.0, 1/d):       -0.067 (near-zero — per-image variance dominates)
  New model (C=0.78, 1/sqrt(d)): -0.065 (~same)
  Improvement is in shape (no high-d under-prediction), not residual variance.

